#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bsq — slim bot-squad CLI for agents (T-0146).

One binary, kubectl-style verbs, that wrap the bot-squad worker-socket
actions so agents stop hand-rolling curl + tmux send-keys. `bsq --help`
is the canonical reference — AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md points here.

Verbs:
  bsq inbox check [--since TS]      drain this session's peer inbox
  bsq inbox wait  [--timeout N]     opt-in long-poll (the bg-watcher mode)
  bsq peer send <to> <text>         peer_send + nudge the recipient pane
  bsq tg ping <message>             explicitly DM the stakeholder (T-0155)
  bsq task new <title> --provenance <src>  allocate next T-NNNN + stub (atomic — T-0174; --provenance REQUIRED)
  bsq task digest                   short backlog digest for the TG chat (T-0589)
  bsq doc new <category> <title>   allocate next D-NNNN + stub doc (T-0172)
  bsq uc new <title>               allocate next UC-NNNN + stub use case
  bsq flow new <uc-id> <title>     allocate next UF-NNNN + stub flow (T-0173)
  bsq initiative new <name>        allocate next T-NNNN + stub kind:initiative task (T-0480)
  bsq spawn <ticket> [--bundle ids] spawn a dev session (auto-resumes an expert)
  bsq cluster-launch <seed>        seed a problem → suggest a similar cluster → launch ONE bundled session (T-0487)
  bsq expert find <ticket>          rank resumable 'pro' sessions for a ticket
  bsq team status                   list this project's sessions
  bsq team list                     list persisted Team rosters (T-0142)
  bsq team archive <sid>            true-archive a session (suspend + archive)
  bsq team resurrect <sid>          bring a session back (unarchive + resume)
  bsq team rename <sid> <name>      rename a session (tmux + UI + registry sync)
  bsq compact [--sid SID]           send /compact to a session (self by default)
  bsq compact-save "<state>"        write your forward-state to your role artifact (compact handoff)
  bsq postpone [--for SECS]         defer your ~1h cache-window recycle one window (repeatable)
  bsq drive off/on/status           operator-only: your own drive continuity toggle (T-0655)
  bsq commit -m MSG <files..>       stage explicit paths + safe-commit

Conventions shared with the other ops shims:
  - $BOT_SQUAD       install root (default /home/www/bot-squad)
  - $WORKER_SOCK     worker unix socket
  - slug is resolved from $PWD against config/projects.toml
  - this session's SID is read from tmux (override with --sid / --from)
"""
